# Script and shot list — "The Paper Lantern" (target 20.0 s at 24 fps = 480 frames)

Style for every image: soft painterly storybook illustration, dusk turning to night; deep blue/violet sky, warm orange lantern glow as the brightest point of each frame. 16:9, 1280x720 (or larger, scaled down).
The child and the lantern follow the production designer's continuity bible (`world/production-designer` `design/`; child: short dark-brown bob, light-blue coat, muted red scarf, charcoal trousers, brown shoes; ivory cuboid paper lantern on a small wooden floating base, warm amber glow), identical in every shot. Palette: indigo/amber dusk.

| # | Time | Shot | Camera move | Picture | Sound |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| T | 0.0–2.5 s | Opening title | fade in from black, hold | "The Paper Lantern" (editor's typography) over a calm dusk river/sky plate from production-designer | ambience fades in; music begins softly |
| 1 | 2.5–6.0 s | Wide: the child kneels at the riverbank at dusk holding the glowing lantern; village roofs in the background | slow push in | the child and lantern clearly visible | water lapping, evening crickets |
| 2 | 6.0–9.5 s | Close: the child's hands set the lantern on the water | slow push in or slight tilt down | lantern touches the water, ripples, reflection | soft water touch |
| 3 | 9.5–13.5 s | Medium/wide: the lantern drifts along the river past the village houses with lit windows | slow pan following the drift | lantern smaller, village lights reflected | river, distant evening |
| 4 | 13.5–17.0 s | Very wide: the river runs to the night horizon; the lantern is a tiny warm light among reflected and real stars | slow tilt up / pull out so the lantern ends as one small light among the stars | lantern a small light among the stars | music swells gently, then settles |
| E | 17.0–20.0 s | End card | dissolve from shot 4's starry sky, fade to black at the end | "The End" in the title's lettering over a night-sky plate | music resolves, ambience fades out |

Transitions: soft dissolves (about 0.5 s) between shots; shot 4 dissolves into the end card on the stars so the lantern's light hands over to the night sky.

Split of making: production-designer makes the stills and the finished silent 1280x720 24 fps shots with the camera moves (each with ~0.5 s handles at both ends for dissolves), the title/end plates and the shot log; editor makes the title/end typography, the timeline and transitions, all sound and the render. Four shots are planned; a fifth is not required; four to six shots in total are allowed, and timing may shift by up to ±1 s per shot as long as the total stays 18–22 s and the order of story beats holds. Cuts may be dissolves.
